  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "De Charentenay entered the marine sector through specialist journalism and press relations for the Rodriguez Group. Work in chartering, sales and management followed, but his path then moved offshore: records place him successively as deckhand, bosun, skipper and first officer. Two years aboard a large motor vessel took him through the Mediterranean, Caribbean, Bahamas and United States and across the Atlantic.\n\nThat operational grounding later informed broader client-facing responsibilities. De Charentenay served as sales manager for the major Cannes pleasure-boat exhibition while continuing professional command work. Marketplace records now place him with a French Riviera brokerage, where he combines hands-on seamanship with international marine sales and represents more than one hundred active listings from Cannes.",
